          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01KDmk8PQySF2YiuJCW5AU1t",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/write-ahead-logging.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Write-Ahead Logging (WAL)\\ndescription: A durability technique in database engines that appends changes to a sequential log before applying them to data pages.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Durability\\n  - concept/Database-Internals\\n  - pattern/WAL\\nconfidence: high\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Clear, technical definition from a reliable source describing an established database pattern.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nWrite-Ahead Logging (WAL) is a fundamental durability mechanism in database engines. Every change to the database is appended to a sequential log file *before* being applied to the main data pages. If a crash occurs between the log write and the page write, recovery proceeds by replaying the log from the last checkpoint.\\n\\n## How It Works\\n\\n1. **Log append**: A change (insert, update, delete) is written to the sequential log file first.\\n2. **Page update**: The change is eventually applied to the main data pages.\\n3. **Crash recovery**: If the system crashes between steps 1 and 2, replay the log to recover the state up to the last checkpoint.\\n\\n## Trade-offs\\n\\n**Benefit:**\\n- **Durability without full-page flushes**: The database gains crash-safety guarantees without forcing every transaction to immediately flush a complete data page to disk, which would be expensive.\\n\\n**Cost:**\\n- **Write amplification**: Each change is written twice \\u2014 once to the log and once eventually to the data page. This incurs additional I/O overhead.\\n\\n## Related Concepts\\n\\n- [[durability]] \\u2014 the guarantee WAL provides\\n- [[crash-recovery]] \\u2014 the mechanism enabled by WAL\\n- [[checkpoints]] \\u2014 the periodic synchronization points from which WAL recovery begins\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Source document on Write-Ahead Logging fundamentals (eval://log-paragraph-specificity/sample-01)\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
